[{:db/id "q-351687/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "838d6a74-d19a-5936-9a7e-ac544df9ed0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351687/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8682be63-22a6-5e12-b2a0-4f9fd2264a64" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351687/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-351687/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351687" :question/id #uuid "ab881a01-81b9-5d9d-8b14-42a587506d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-351687" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{5}^{n}(x-4)^{n}}{n!}=5(x-4)+\\frac{{5}^{2}(x-4)^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{5}^{3}(x-4)^{3}}{3!}+⋯\\,.\n$$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test, we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{5}^{n}(x-4)^{n}}{n!}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{\\frac{{5}^{n+1}(x-4)^{n+1}}{(n+1)!}}{\\frac{{5}^{n}(x-4)^{n}}{n!}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{5}^{n+1}(x-4)^{n+1}}{(n+1)!}\\cdot \\frac{n!}{{5}^{n}(x-4)^{n}}| \\\\  & =5|x-4|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{n+1} \\\\  & =5|x-4|\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied for all $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$  Therefore, we conclude that the radius of convergence is $R=\\infty .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351687/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347518/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3795b54f-da90-54dc-8a10-266a69ca402b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347518/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7144038d-dd10-5ea5-b1f0-45ee26e61224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347518/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e1cd048-cae9-5ec7-b039-4274121ca87d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347518/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-347518/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-347518/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347518" :question/id #uuid "0405c58c-7f2f-5ecf-8149-deaa96d59971" :question/math-academy-id "q-347518" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{n}^{3}(x-2)^{n}=(x-2)+{2}^{3}(x-2)^{2}+{3}^{3}(x-2)^{3}+⋯\\,.\n$$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test, we define ${a}_{n}={n}^{3}(x-2)^{n}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(n+1)^{3}(x-2)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}(x-2)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(n+1)^{3}(x-2)}{{n}^{3}}| \\\\  & =|x-2|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n+1}{n})}^{3} \\\\  & =|x-2|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x-2|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied if $|x-2|<1.$ Therefore, we conclude that the radius of convergence is $R=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-347518/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347518"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351676/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "fa4c3e89-4448-5ea6-8426-ab2d19d501d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351676/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d049e1-070d-5be4-ab4c-097fff07e8f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351676/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-351676/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351676" :question/id #uuid "f8fa7605-655f-54c8-a564-192b8ff7cd04" :question/math-academy-id "q-351676" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{n}^{2}(2x-6)^{n}=(2x-6)+{2}^{2}(2x-6)^{2}+{3}^{2}(2x-6)^{3}+⋯\\,.\n$$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test, we define ${a}_{n}={n}^{2}(2x-6)^{n}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(n+1)^{2}(2x-6)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}(2x-6)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(n+1)^{2}(2x-6)}{{n}^{2}}| \\\\  & =|2x-6|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n+1}{n})}^{2} \\\\  & =|2x-6|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|2x-6| \\\\  & =2|x-3|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied if $|x-3|<\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore, we conclude that the radius of convergence is $R=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351676/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617/selection/8beee86ea931f536f05e8808030c4cf83bdbbc410eb7a15e1e5f39fe305fdc6e" :answer/id #uuid "da99dddb-2120-5ac8-9524-bbbcf8804f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617/selection/d3b00a08c83aec868e8a4d3a5aff2a960bdde681558a660cd6f4c4c969d7dde9" :answer/id #uuid "496603ab-7b03-5d50-b8bc-b08f42c2078e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617/selection/bcb3a13c00508924772cd99f87896054b10639a22a6eee40c385ea4e630fbe24" :answer/id #uuid "75eff5fc-4e24-5da9-9166-73a2c6afaa00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617/selection/f970a95b2ce9bd563f661045c30e6a55f907c688f1d23c77f97fa3e63a89ac5c" :answer/id #uuid "4db7fd9b-afdc-598f-a192-7caee1041340" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617/selection/fe472ff3ff70f2b497884848b58a844440c390a3db40d74604ce5e927b13e9a8" :answer/id #uuid "145aecc8-53f1-5c38-b2d4-243065a3d9c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "64ce531b-7e10-56c7-9118-80ebc55ef4cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10617/selection/d3b00a08c83aec868e8a4d3a5aff2a960bdde681558a660cd6f4c4c969d7dde9" :answer-field/choices ["q-10617/selection/8beee86ea931f536f05e8808030c4cf83bdbbc410eb7a15e1e5f39fe305fdc6e" "q-10617/selection/d3b00a08c83aec868e8a4d3a5aff2a960bdde681558a660cd6f4c4c969d7dde9" "q-10617/selection/bcb3a13c00508924772cd99f87896054b10639a22a6eee40c385ea4e630fbe24" "q-10617/selection/f970a95b2ce9bd563f661045c30e6a55f907c688f1d23c77f97fa3e63a89ac5c" "q-10617/selection/fe472ff3ff70f2b497884848b58a844440c390a3db40d74604ce5e927b13e9a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10617" :question/id #uuid "b81c79bc-0ed8-5e82-89af-c585b2146925" :question/math-academy-id "q-10617" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-3)^{n}}{(2n)!}=1+\\frac{(x-3)}{2!}+\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4!}+\\frac{(x-3)^{3}}{6!}+⋯\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test. we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(x-3)^{n}}{(2n)!}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x-3)^{n+1}}{[2(n+1)]!}\\cdot \\frac{(2n)!}{(x-3)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x-3)}{(2n+2)(2n+1)}| \\\\  & =|x-3|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n+2)(2n+1)} \\\\  & =|x-3|\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied for all $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$ Therefore, we conclude that the radius of convergence is $R=\\infty .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-10617/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769/selection/fe472ff3ff70f2b497884848b58a844440c390a3db40d74604ce5e927b13e9a8" :answer/id #uuid "b423037d-512e-5010-b057-468ff8c591cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769/selection/bcb3a13c00508924772cd99f87896054b10639a22a6eee40c385ea4e630fbe24" :answer/id #uuid "cc13cd55-472b-5973-b773-2a76d71ba741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769/selection/d3b00a08c83aec868e8a4d3a5aff2a960bdde681558a660cd6f4c4c969d7dde9" :answer/id #uuid "a5cd127c-357b-575e-8041-3246461a5570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769/selection/fdfdeb2a3fb0839b55b5fb00cc8369f44c7cf412862bdd3352882dfaf7213dda" :answer/id #uuid "924ade29-3101-5c6a-a141-cd45a853c3b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769/selection/f970a95b2ce9bd563f661045c30e6a55f907c688f1d23c77f97fa3e63a89ac5c" :answer/id #uuid "cf2151c9-b86f-5428-8b59-8c629864b6e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a75143a-08f0-51ff-a346-2f75eb1313c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10769/selection/bcb3a13c00508924772cd99f87896054b10639a22a6eee40c385ea4e630fbe24" :answer-field/choices ["q-10769/selection/fe472ff3ff70f2b497884848b58a844440c390a3db40d74604ce5e927b13e9a8" "q-10769/selection/bcb3a13c00508924772cd99f87896054b10639a22a6eee40c385ea4e630fbe24" "q-10769/selection/d3b00a08c83aec868e8a4d3a5aff2a960bdde681558a660cd6f4c4c969d7dde9" "q-10769/selection/fdfdeb2a3fb0839b55b5fb00cc8369f44c7cf412862bdd3352882dfaf7213dda" "q-10769/selection/f970a95b2ce9bd563f661045c30e6a55f907c688f1d23c77f97fa3e63a89ac5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10769" :question/id #uuid "171d01f5-9643-594d-9774-ce03279c953f" :question/math-academy-id "q-10769" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{n}^{2}(x+1)^{n}=(x+1)+{2}^{2}(x+1)^{2}+{3}^{2}(x+1)^{3}+⋯\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test. we define ${a}_{n}={n}^{2}(x+1)^{n}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(n+1)^{2}(x+1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}(x+1)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(n+1)^{2}(x+1)}{{n}^{2}}| \\\\  & =|x+1|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n+1}{n})}^{2} \\\\  & =|x+1|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x+1|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied if $|x+1|<1.$ Therefore, we conclude that the radius of convergence is $R=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-10769/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3ddb23e1-aba7-533f-ac75-45e042ae1480" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7aed96d5-f9bb-5be8-a913-b6428c242885" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "efc246e8-1e16-55de-b61c-9ca0286790d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b4a46b86-5b05-5910-9b3f-d2ef575aed27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "8926754f-4116-5e23-8d1d-e8707cf0e04d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "46580640-eb3e-5da4-a467-e7469de35192" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50876/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-50876/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-50876/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-50876/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-50876/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-50876/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50876" :question/id #uuid "2d87eb27-cda9-59e9-b285-2428cd7d1a82" :question/math-academy-id "q-50876" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+1)^{n}$ converges at  $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=-3$\n- The series converges at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}$\n- The series converges at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-1,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{5}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{5}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041629/assets/57208948dece1112674d3578763bc8d6b73d1d6ab91d160b14839e16a39cf2f6.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $-3\\in (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-\\frac{7}{2}\\notin (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $2\\notin (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-50876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "52071ca4-4b43-5106-8633-a2d44d3f5413" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b0f5e8cf-6dce-5eee-b1e6-3dce3d680111" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "bf56e9c0-709e-54f3-84a0-bd199e2467b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d64e5778-7876-5394-80a1-94e585be9d64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "173b92d5-de52-5053-800d-f844e3589aa5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "621b4bd5-2f8e-501c-bbca-acd74976533f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50874/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-50874/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-50874/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-50874/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-50874/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-50874/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50874" :question/id #uuid "e2ea9b3f-0969-5fc9-ae5d-18723a91ce29" :question/math-academy-id "q-50874" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+1)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-4,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series diverges at $x=-5$\n- The series converges at $x=2$\n- The series converges at $x=-3$" :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-1,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-4,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $3,$ i.e., $R\\ge 3.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-4,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-4,2).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041629/assets/a246a6460d15037b469072b4275e51ff4dd9c56242f6ffeae1bebc2adf66f39f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-5\\notin [-4,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $2\\notin [-4,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $-3\\in [-4,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-50874/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50874"] :db/ensure 